  "title": "Kirby Problem 1.74",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "How does ropelength behave under connected sum of knots?\nHere are two conjectures, the second a weakening of the first.\n(a) For any knot or link types $K_{1}$ and $K_{2}$,\nRop $(K_{1}\\#K_{2}) \\leq$ Rop $(K_{1}) +$ Rop $(K_{2}) - (4\\pi - 4).$\n(b) For any knot or link types $K_{1}$ and $K_{2}$,\n\n$$\nRop(K_{1}\\#K_{2}) \\leq Rop(K_{1}) + Rop(K_{2}) - c,\n$$\n\nwhere $c > 0$ is some constant independent of knot type.",
